<title>USA: U.S. Gulf rigs unchanged at 167 in week.</title>
<headline>U.S. Gulf rigs unchanged at 167 in week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>There were 167 rigs under contract in the U.S. Gulf as of April 18, up one from the period ending April 11, Offshore Data Services said Friday.</p>
<p>The utilization rate for rigs working in the Gulf, based on a total fleet of 179, remained 93.3 percent.</p>
<p>The number of working rigs in the European/Mediterranean area remained unchanged at 103 rigs under contract out of a total fleet of 104, a utilization rate of 99.0 pct.</p>
<p>The worldwide rig count was unchanged at 574 out of a total fleet of 604, with a utilization rate of 95.0 percent, up 0.01.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk 212-859-1620</p>
</text>
